&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Full Name:&lt;/strong&gt; Dr. Ali Mustafa Kamelov&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;by [[*user ]]&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
				<pubDate>Sun, 08 Jul 2012 03:18:12 +0000</pubDate>
												<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p><strong>Full Name:</strong> Dr. Ali Mustafa Kamelov</p> <p><strong>Security Clearance:</strong> Level 4</p> <p><strong>Location:</strong> Site 437</p> <p><strong>Area(s) of Expertise:</strong> Anomalous crystallography, janitorial sciences, <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">agricultural and biological sciences</span>, temporal paradox management</p> <p><strong>History:</strong> Born in Kazan in 1891, Dr. Kamelov received a degree in Art History from Moscow State University in 1914, followed by a PhD in Theoretical Physics in 1922. In 1924, he was selected by the Soviet government to join the fledgling Committee For The Investigation of Anomalous Phenomenon as Assistant Custodian. Over the course of the next decade, he rose to the rank of Chief Director for Central Asian and Custodial Affairs. In 1934, Dr. Kamelov was recruited to the Foundation by Agent ██████. In addition to other duties, since 1981, he has been responsible for the maintenance of the &quot;Groups of Interest&quot; entry on <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/groups-of-interest#toc18">the Office for the Reclamation of Islamic Artifacts (ORIA)</a>.</p> <p>Due to the cumulative effects of over ██ years of constant chain smoking, Dr. Kamelov's office is to be considered a Class Two chemohazard.</p> <p><strong>Note:</strong> Due to Dr. Kamelov's ongoing obsession with Lysenkoism and refusal to accept modern genetic theory, all reports with relevant information regarding genetics and/or evolution are to be edited by Junior Researcher Gaffney. Under no circumstances is Dr. Kamelov to be made aware of this arrangement.</p> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">SCP Reports Complied</span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1316">SCP-1316</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1474">SCP-1474</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1605">SCP-1605</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-1832">SCP-1832</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2009">SCP-2009</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2214">SCP-2214</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2387">SCP-2387</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2443">SCP-2443</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3967">SCP-3967</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4884">SCP-4884</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4083">SCP-4083</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4146">SCP-4146</a></li> </ul> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Additional Documentation</span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/notes-towards-a-manifesto">Notes Towards A Manifesto</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/broadcast">Broadcast</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/dragon-s-teeth">Dragon's Teeth</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/father-iron">Father Iron</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/purity-of-essence">Purity Of Essence</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/there-was-one-there-was-not-one">There Was One There Was Not One</a> (Part of the <em>Only Game In Town</em> canon)</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-end">The End</a> (Part of the <em>Only Game In Town</em> canon)</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/now-this">Now This</a> (Part of the <em>Competitive Eschatology</em> canon)</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/what-did-i-come-down-here-for">What Did I Come Down Here For?</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/a-kind-of-christmas">A Kind Of Christmas</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/going-out-of-book">Going Out Of Book</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/a-burial-in-the-woods">A Burial In The Woods</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/smothering-dreams">Smothering Dreams</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/nope-not-typing-all-that">Site 11, Conference Room K, 8:58 AM, July 12, 1982</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/cleon">Cleon</a> (Part of the <em>Coldest War</em> canon)</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/17-luxemburg-prospekt">17 Luxemburg Prospekt</a></li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/the-king-in-chains">The King In Chains</a> (Part of the <em>Only Game In Town</em> canon)</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/on-the-origins">On The Origins of Pre-Modern Fleshspeaking Rituals</a> (Part of the <em>Only Game In Town</em> canon) (co-authored with <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/riemann" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1787775&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609384707" alt="Riemann" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1787775)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/riemann" >Riemann</a></span>)</li> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/barker">Barker</a></li> </ul> <p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Passive-Aggressive Notes Sent</span></p> <ul> <li><a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-885-j">SCP-885-J</a></li> </ul> <p><a href="http://scp-sandbox-3.wikidot.com/gaffsey-scp">Found in Dr. Kamelov's waste bin</a></p> <p>by [[*user ]]</p> 
